Dear Nimble devs,<br><br>For a compiled Nimble MCMC run, I have `monitors2` set to one particular vector variable &#39;K[1:30]&#39;, which holds the cluster number occupation of 30 datapoints. In the MCMC run I have the arguments<br><br>...<br>niter = 1024,<br>thin2 = 1024,<br>...<br><br>so that &#39;K&#39; is only saved during the last MCMC step. A slice sampler is used for &#39;K&#39;, and in the Nimble configuration output I correctly see<br><br>```<br>...<br>===== Samplers =====<br>slice sampler (31)<br>...<br>   - K[]  (30 elements)<br>...<br>```<br><br><br>All works fine, but I notice a quirk when I eventually try to access `mvSamples2`. If I access it with `as.matrix()`, then &#39;K&#39; is correctly given as a 30-element vector. But if I access it with `as.list()`, then &#39;K&#39; is incorrectly given as a single scalar. Here is a snippet of debugging lines inserted into the code:<br><br>```<br>cat(&#39;
Now as matrix:
&#39;)<br>str(as.matrix(Cmcsampler$mvSamples2))<br>cat(&#39;
Now as list:
&#39;)<br>str(as.list(Cmcsampler$mvSamples2))<br>cat(&#39;
***
&#39;)<br>```<br><br>and here is the corresponding output:<br><br>```<br>Now as matrix:<br>num [1, 1:30] 46 46 46 46 45 46 46 45 45 46 ...<br>  - attr(*, &quot;dimnames&quot;)=List of 2<br>   ..$ : NULL<br>   ..$ : chr [1:30] &quot;K[1]&quot; &quot;K[2]&quot; &quot;K[3]&quot; &quot;K[4]&quot; ...<br><br>Now as list:<br>List of 1<br>  $ K: num [1, 1] 46<br><br>***<br>```<br><br>Sorry for not sending a minimal example yet. I was wondering whether it&#39;s maybe straightforward for you to check for a possible bug in the Nimble code about this. My guess is that something happen because there&#39;s only one MCMC sample of &#39;K&#39;. If it&#39;s best for you to have a minimal working example, I&#39;m happy to prepare one!<br><br>Cheers,<br>Luca<br>
